@startuml Spiritbound-Core-Data-Model
' Spiritbound — Core Data Model
' Source of truth for SpacetimeDB tables. Diagram is human-readable;
' the same entities map ~1:1 to SpacetimeDB tables (TS server module).
'
' Conventions:
'   {PK} primary key      {FK} foreign key      {derived} computed in rules/, NOT stored
'   Types are illustrative (SpacetimeDB/TS): Identity, u32, u64, f32, bool, String, Timestamp, enum
'
' Layering (see architect skill): tables hold STATE only. All rules
' (scaling, merge results, retention rolls, attunement limits) live in pure
' rules/ functions and are shown here as {derived} or in notes.

skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle
title Spiritbound — Core Data Model
!theme vibrant

' ============================================================
' ENUMS
' ============================================================
package "Enums" <<Frame>> {
  enum Rarity {
    COMMON
    UNCOMMON
    RARE
    EPIC
    LEGENDARY
  }
  enum CardType {
    ACTIVE
    PASSIVE
  }
  enum PassiveKind {
    WARD       ' protective: mitigation / shield / resist
    TRIGGERED  ' fires on a condition, e.g. every 3rd hit
  }
  enum StatType {
    PHYSICAL_ATTACK
    MAGIC_ATTACK
    ' extensible: e.g. a HEALING tag scaling off magic_attack x healing_boost
  }
  enum DamageSchool {
    PHYSICAL
    MAGICAL
    ' the actual enum used in code (index.ts TSchool) for CardDefinition.scaling_school
    ' and ItemDefinition.weapon_school; distinct from the StatType tag above.
  }
  enum EquipSlot {
    HEAD
    CHEST
    HANDS
    LEGS
    BOOTS
    MAIN_HAND
    OFF_HAND
    NECKLACE
    RING       ' 2 ring slots
    EARRING    ' 2 earring slots
  }
  enum ItemCategory {
    EQUIPMENT
    CONSUMABLE ' potions
    REVIVAL    ' Soul Ember — non-tradeable, prevents next death
    QUEST
    MATERIAL   ' crafting / merge fuel
    DUNGEON_KEY ' Hollow Keys for endgame dungeon tiers
  }
  enum ShapeType {
    CONE       ' dagger = short + skinny
    LINE       ' spear / bow = long + thin
    ARC        ' sword = medium width
    CIRCLE     ' staff = large area
  }
  enum ArmorWeight {
    CLOTH      ' biases magic_def
    CHAIN      ' balanced
    PLATE      ' biases physical_def
    ' bias telegraph only; anyone can wear anything (full-plate mage is legal)
  }
  enum AggroState {
    IDLE
    CHASING
    CASTING
    COOLDOWN
    RESETTING
  }
}

' ============================================================
' VALUE OBJECT
' ============================================================
package "Value Objects" <<Frame>> {
  class StatBlock <<value object>> {
    ' --- Primary attributes (race-seeded; the only innate lean) ---
    power : i32          ' -> physical_attack
    knowledge : i32      ' -> magic_attack
    health : i32         ' -> max_hp, hp_regen
    will : i32           ' -> max_mp, mp_regen, magic_resist, healing_boost
    agility : i32        ' -> evasion, parry, attack_speed
    precision : i32      ' -> accuracy, magic_accuracy, crit
    ' --- Resource maxes (current HP/MP live on Character) ---
    max_hp : i32
    hp_regen : f32
    max_mp : i32
    mp_regen : f32
    move_speed : f32     ' multiplier; 1.0 = base
    ' --- Offensive ---
    weapon_damage : i32  ' WEAPON-ONLY; base for basic attacks
    physical_attack : i32 ' boosts physical-tag cards
    magic_attack : i32    ' boosts magic-tag cards (and healing)
    attack_speed : f32    ' multiplier, higher = faster (NOT Aion's inverted convention)
    casting_speed : f32   ' multiplier, higher = faster
    physical_crit : f32
    magic_crit : f32
    accuracy : i32        ' counters target evasion / parry
    magic_accuracy : i32  ' counters target magic_resist
    healing_boost : f32   ' scales healing-card output
    ' --- Defensive ---
    physical_def : i32    ' mitigation (plate > chain > cloth)
    magic_def : i32       ' mitigation (cloth highest)
    evasion : f32         ' glancing blow = partial dmg reduction on a connected hit, low cap ~15-20% (NOT full negation)
    parry : f32           ' reduce a connected physical hit, capped
    block : f32           ' off-hand shield reduce
    magic_resist : f32    ' negate connected magic hit / resist 2ndary effects, capped
    ' sources stack additively; any field may be 0
  }
}

' ============================================================
' LOGIN / ACCOUNT  (login server owns credentials; module trusts identity)
' ============================================================
package "Account & Identity" <<Frame>> {
  class Account {
    identity : Identity {PK}   ' issued by login server
    display_name : String
    created_at : Timestamp
  }
}

' ============================================================
' CONTENT / DEFINITIONS  (static-ish design content)
' ============================================================
package "Definitions (content)" <<Frame>> {
  class Race {
    race_id : u32 {PK}
    name : String
    base_stats : StatBlock
    description : String
  }

  class CardDefinition {
    card_def_id : u32 {PK}
    name : String
    rarity : Rarity
    card_type : CardType
    passive_kind : PassiveKind   ' null when ACTIVE
    scaling_tag : StatType       ' which stat its power reads from
    base_shape : ShapeType       ' weapon then MODIFIES this geometry
    base_power : f32             ' scaled by character level {see note}
    base_cooldown : f32
    mp_cost : i32
    min_character_level : u32    ' level gate to EQUIP (kept thru death, re-earned)
                                  ' ALSO gates drop eligibility (killer's level), see note
    flavor : String              ' lore-keeper domain
  }

  class ItemDefinition {
    item_def_id : u64 {PK}       ' autoInc
    slug : String                ' unique; idempotency key for seedItems (mirrors CardDefinition)
    name : String
    rarity : Rarity
    category : ItemCategory
    slot : EquipSlot {optional}          ' null unless EQUIPMENT
    armor_weight : ArmorWeight {optional} ' armor pieces only; bias telegraph, NOT a wear gate
    ' weapon-only (MAIN_HAND) — all four optional, all required together:
    weapon_school : DamageSchool {optional}  ' what stat school it feeds to cards
    geometry_shape : ShapeType {optional}    ' how it bends a card's base_shape
    geometry_width : f32 {optional}          ' wider = more area, less focus
    geometry_range : f32 {optional}          ' also bends reach (melee swing on a staff reaches further)
    min_level : u32               ' level gate on drop eligibility (killer's level); default 1
    stat_modifiers : StatBlock   ' additive stats this item grants (missing fields = 0, not 1.0)
    flavor : String              ' lore-keeper domain
  }

  class SpiritDefinition {
    spirit_def_id : u32 {PK}
    name : String
    level : u32
    rarity_ceiling : Rarity      ' max card rarity it can swap
    allows_merge : bool
    zone_id : u32 {FK}           ' location spirits are world-placed
    flavor : String              ' lore-keeper domain
  }

  class Zone {
    zone_id : u32 {PK}
    name : String
    min_level : u32              ' soft/hard gating = open question
    max_level : u32
    description : String
  }

  class DungeonDefinition {
    dungeon_id : u32 {PK}
    name : String
    tier : u32                   ' 1=Delve 2=Vault 3=Abyss 4=Hollow
    hollow_subtier : u32         ' 0 unless tier=4; HollowI=1, HollowII=2 ...
    recommended_level : u32
    min_players : u32            ' 1 = soloable
    max_players : u32
    requires_key : bool          ' Hollow tiers need a DungeonKey item
    zone_id : u32 {FK}           ' where the entrance lives in the world
  }

  class AccountMilestone {
    milestone_id : u32 {PK}
    name : String
    threshold_account_xp : u64   ' total XP across all lives to unlock
    reward_type : String         ' TUTORIAL_SKIP / RACE_UNLOCK / VAULT_SLOT / COSMETIC
    reward_ref : String          ' e.g. race_id, cosmetic_id, or "vault+1"
  }
}

' ============================================================
' RUNTIME / INSTANCES  (per-account & per-life state)
' ============================================================
package "Runtime (instances)" <<Frame>> {

  class AccountProgress {
    account_identity : Identity {FK} {PK}
    total_xp_all_lives : u64          ' accumulates across every character death
    tutorial_completed : bool         ' gates the level-10 skip on next life
    unlocked_milestone_ids : u32[]    ' which AccountMilestones are claimed
    ' NOTE: no legacy vault — personal spirit is the SOLE cross-death card
    ' retention mechanism. bond_xp never resets; spirit grows across all lives.
  }

  class PersonalSpirit {
    spirit_id : u64 {PK}
    account_identity : Identity {FK}  ' 1:1 with Account, PERSISTS across deaths
    name : String
    level : u32
    bond_xp : u64                     ' grows by sacrificing cards
    active_slots : u32 {derived}      ' hand active-card slots (start 2), from level
    passive_slots : u32 {derived}     ' hand passive-card slots (start 1), from level
    attunement_by_rarity : map<Rarity,u32> {derived} ' rarity-tiered death-save slots
    ' e.g. {COMMON:3, RARE:1, LEGENDARY:0} at low level -> can't hoard 10 legendaries
  }

  class Character {
    character_id : u64 {PK}
    account_identity : Identity {FK}
    race_id : u32 {FK}
    level : u32
    xp : u64
    zone_id : u32 {FK}
    pos_x : f32
    pos_y : f32
    current_hp : i32
    current_mp : i32                  ' active cards cost MP; can't pay => won't fire
    alive : bool                      ' false = permadeath; new Character created
    created_at : Timestamp
    died_at : Timestamp               ' null while alive
    last_level_up_at : Timestamp {optional} ' set by _grantXp on a level increase; client watches this to trigger the level-up flash
    effective_stats : StatBlock {derived} ' race base + equipped gear, in rules/
  }

  class CardInstance {
    card_instance_id : u64 {PK}
    owner_identity : Identity {FK}    ' ACCOUNT-owned -> survives death, tradeable
    card_def_id : u32 {FK}
    merge_level : u32                 ' adds EFFECTS, not raw numbers
    attuned : bool                    ' guaranteed-survive; count <= spirit slots
    scaled_power : f32 {derived}      ' base_power x char level curve, in rules/
  }

  class EquippedCard {
    character_id : u64 {FK}           ' the current life's HAND (the "deck")
    card_instance_id : u64 {FK}
    slot_type : CardType              ' ACTIVE (max 10) or PASSIVE (max 5)
    slot_index : u32
    ' separate from inventory; changed only at a spirit
  }

  class ItemInstance {
    item_instance_id : u64 {PK}
    owner_character_id : u64 {FK}     ' CHARACTER-owned -> LOST on death (body)
    item_def_id : u64 {FK}
    quantity : u32                    ' 1 for equipment, stackable for consumables/materials
    ' table(public: true) — required for InventoryPanel/CharacterSheet to subscribe.
    ' No row-level security yet: any client can subscribe to every character's bag,
    ' same exposure as the pre-existing CardInstance. See ARCHITECTURE.md.
  }

  class EquippedItem {
    character_id : u64 {FK}
    item_instance_id : u64 {FK}
    slot : EquipSlot
    slot_ordinal : u32               ' 0/1 for the two rings & two earrings
    ' table(public: true) — same visibility note as ItemInstance above.
  }

  class CardDrop {
    drop_id : u64 {PK}               ' autoInc
    card_def_id : u32 {FK}
    zone_id : u32 {FK}
    pos_x : f32
    pos_y : f32
    created_at : Timestamp
    ' despawns 60s after created_at (cardDropCleanup, every 10s); pickup within 80px
  }

  class ItemDrop {
    item_drop_id : u64 {PK}          ' autoInc
    item_def_id : u64 {FK}
    zone_id : u32 {FK}
    pos_x : f32
    pos_y : f32
    created_at : Timestamp
    ' same lifecycle as CardDrop, swept by the same cardDropCleanup reducer.
    ' ITEM_DROP_CHANCE (20%) roll per enemy death, independent of the card roll;
    ' rarity-weighted + min_level-gated by killer's level, see N_Leveling note.
  }

  class Enemy {
    enemy_id : u64 {PK}              ' autoInc
    zone_id : u32 {FK}
    pos_x : f32
    pos_y : f32
    spawn_x : f32
    spawn_y : f32
    current_hp : i32
    max_hp : i32
    alive : bool
    damage_per_hit : i32
    attack_range_px : f32
    attack_cooldown_seconds : f32
    last_attack_at : Timestamp {optional}
    aggro_state : AggroState
    target_character_id : u64 {optional}
    last_seen_target_at : Timestamp {optional}
    cast_started_at : Timestamp {optional}
    cast_duration_seconds : f32
    cast_shape : ShapeType
    cast_damage : i32
    xp_reward : u64                  ' awarded to the killer via _grantXp; 25 default for zone-1
  }
}

' ============================================================
' SOCIAL  (groups & alliances; over ACTIVE characters)
' Build order: deferred — not needed for the vertical slice.
' ============================================================
package "Social" <<Frame>> {
  class Group {
    group_id : u64 {PK}
    leader_character_id : u64 {FK}
    created_at : Timestamp
    ' size 2..6 enforced in rules
  }
  class GroupMember {
    group_id : u64 {FK}
    character_id : u64 {FK}           ' active life; dead char leaves, re-invite new one
  }
  class Alliance {
    alliance_id : u64 {PK}
    created_at : Timestamp
    ' up to 6 Groups (<=36 players). OPEN: transient coalition vs persistent guild;
    ' persistent social identity should live at ACCOUNT level, not here.
  }
  class AllianceGroup {
    alliance_id : u64 {FK}
    group_id : u64 {FK}
  }
}

' ============================================================
' SETS  (item set bonuses)
' ============================================================
package "Sets (content)" <<Frame>> {
  class SetDefinition {
    set_id : u32 {PK}
    name : String
    description : String
    soulbound : bool             ' if true: full set survives death (held by spirit)
    ' Whisp Sets: extremely rare; the only gear exception to "all gear lost on death"
    ' Only triggers if ALL set pieces are equipped at time of death
  }
  class SetBonus {
    set_id : u32 {FK}
    pieces_required : u32             ' 2 / 4 / 6 ... tiered
    bonus_stats : StatBlock           ' feeds cards -> item-balancer seam
    bonus_effect : String             ' non-stat effects
  }
}

' ============================================================
' CARD GRAPH  (combos + evolution = "skill-tree depth" without point-buy)
' ============================================================
package "Card Graph (content)" <<Frame>> {
  class CardChainLink {
    predecessor_def_id : u32 {FK}     ' the opener
    successor_def_id : u32 {FK}       ' the follow-up
    window_seconds : f32              ' time after opener to land the chain
    combo_bonus : String              ' bonus when cast in-chain
    ' multiple successors off one opener = branching combos
  }
  class CardEvolution {
    from_def_id : u32 {FK}
    to_def_id : u32 {FK}              ' merge/upgrade target
    branch_label : String             ' e.g. "fire" vs "frost"
    requirement : String              ' catalyst / merge condition
    ' multiple branches off one card = an emergent evolution tree
  }
}

' ============================================================
' RELATIONSHIPS
' ============================================================
Account "1" -- "1" PersonalSpirit : owns >
Account "1" -- "0..*" Character : has (1 alive) >
Account "1" -- "0..*" CardInstance : collection >
Account "1" -- "1" AccountProgress : tracks >

Character "*" -- "1" Race : is a >
Character "1" -- "0..15" EquippedCard : hand (cap 10A/5P; slots from spirit) >
Character "1" -- "0..*" ItemInstance : inventory (lost on death) >
Character "1" -- "0..*" EquippedItem : equipped gear >
Character "*" -- "1" Zone : located in >

PersonalSpirit ..> EquippedCard : grants slot counts

EquippedCard "*" -- "1" CardInstance : references >
EquippedItem "*" -- "1" ItemInstance : references >

CardInstance "*" -- "1" CardDefinition : instance of >
ItemInstance "*" -- "1" ItemDefinition : instance of >

SpiritDefinition "*" -- "1" Zone : placed in >
DungeonDefinition "*" -- "1" Zone : entrance in >

Zone "1" -- "0..*" Enemy : hosts >
Zone "1" -- "0..*" CardDrop : contains >
Zone "1" -- "0..*" ItemDrop : contains >
CardDrop "*" -- "1" CardDefinition : instance of >
ItemDrop "*" -- "1" ItemDefinition : instance of >

' Social
Group "1" -- "2..6" GroupMember : has >
GroupMember "*" -- "1" Character : is >
Alliance "1" -- "0..6" AllianceGroup : federates >
AllianceGroup "*" -- "1" Group : is >

' Sets
SetDefinition "1" -- "1..*" SetBonus : tiers >
' NOTE: ItemDefinition has no set_id yet — sets are still deferred (see Sets package comment).
' Reintroduce "ItemDefinition -- SetDefinition : belongs to" once set membership is implemented.

' Card graph (self-referential over CardDefinition)
CardDefinition "1" -- "0..*" CardChainLink : opener >
CardChainLink "*" -- "1" CardDefinition : successor >
CardDefinition "1" -- "0..*" CardEvolution : evolves from >
CardEvolution "*" -- "1" CardDefinition : evolves to >

Race ..> StatBlock : base_stats
ItemDefinition ..> StatBlock : stat_modifiers
Character ..> StatBlock : effective_stats
SetBonus ..> StatBlock : bonus_stats

' ============================================================
' NOTES — rules & mechanics that are NOT columns
' ============================================================
note bottom of CardInstance
  **Damage in play** = scaled_power(card, character.level)
  evaluated against weapon.weapon_school matching
  card.scaling_school, with shape = base_shape bent by
  weapon geometry_shape / geometry_width / geometry_range.
  Same card: sword = narrow+strong, staff = wide+far+weak.
  Balance rule (ability-balancer): no weapon gives both
  high damage AND wide shape on one card.
  IMPLEMENTED: damageEnemy/applyDamage (index.ts) call
  rules/combat.ts#resolveHit with real effectiveStats on
  both sides (index.ts#buildEffectiveStats) — no more
  client-trusted flat damage numbers. cardDefId 0 in
  damageEnemy means a bare weapon swing (no card): its
  "cardBasePower" is the weapon's own weaponDamage stat.
end note

note bottom of ItemDefinition
  **Content pipeline** (mirrors CardDefinition/cards.json exactly):
  content/equipment.json -> Zod validator (content/validateEquipment.ts)
  -> unit tests (content/equipment.test.ts) -> seedItems reducer,
  upserted by slug (idempotency key), same as seedCards.
  Balance rule (item-balancer, enforced in the validator): a main_hand
  weapon with geometry_width > 1.0 (wide/forgiving) may not also have
  high weapon_damage + physical_attack + magic_attack (narrow = strong,
  wide = weak) — same power-vs-area tradeoff as CardInstance above.
  min_level (validator-enforced, nonnegative int; default 1 for all six
  starter items) gates drop eligibility the same way CardDefinition's
  min_character_level does — see N_Leveling note.
end note

note bottom of PersonalSpirit
  **On death (rules/):** all ItemInstances destroyed.
  CardInstances: attuned cards survive, limited by
  attunement_by_rarity (rarity-tiered, so no hoarding
  10 legendaries). Un-attuned cards are lost. No RNG.
  Spirit is the only thing that crosses the death boundary.
end note

note bottom of EquippedItem
  equipItem/unequipItem (index.ts) recompute maxHp/maxMp before and
  after the gear change and rescale currentHp/currentMp by the same
  ratio (never a hard clamp) via _withProportionalResourceUpdate —
  gaining maxHp always feels like a gain, never a wasted overflow.
end note

note top of EquippedCard
  The "deck". Swapping cards happens ONLY at a spirit
  (location spirit for high rarity; personal spirit for
  minor cards while travelling). Rarity gate = spirit.rarity_ceiling.
end note

note as N_Reducers
  **Reducers (thin) act on these tables:**
  move, cast_ability, basic_attack, take_damage, die,
  pick_up_item, equip_item, equip_card (at spirit),
  merge_cards (3->1), evolve_card (branch), sacrifice_card_to_spirit,
  trade_cards, group_invite/join/leave, alliance_form/join,
  enter_dungeon, use_soul_ember, claim_milestone.
  Each: validate -> call pure rules fn -> write rows.
end note

note as N_Leveling
  **Leveling rules (rules/):**
  IMPLEMENTED: enemy.xp_reward (25 default, zone-1) is granted to the
  killer on death via a shared _grantXp(ctx, character, amount) helper
  (index.ts), used by both damageEnemy and the public grantXp reducer.
  XP gained -> character.xp (per-life); on threshold (computeCharacterLevel)
  -> level up -> currentHp/currentMp refilled to max, last_level_up_at
  stamped (client watches this field to trigger the level-up flash).
  account_progress.total_xp_all_lives += XP always (never resets, survives
  death — verified across a real death+respawn cycle).
  computeCharacterLevel is duplicated byte-for-byte in
  client/src/levelCurve.ts so the client's XP bar never disagrees with the
  server — see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md for the duplication risk/rationale.
  On death: check AccountMilestone thresholds -> auto-claim new milestones.
  tutorial_completed at level 10 -> unlocks level-10 start for next char.
  Soul Ember (REVIVAL item): on take_damage -> if would_die and ember in
  inventory -> consume ember, set hp=1. Non-tradeable enforced in rules.
  Revive card (TRIGGERED passive): fires on group member death IN dungeon
  only; once per dungeon instance; cannot target self.

  **Drop gating (IMPLEMENTED, index.ts):** CARD_DROP_CHANCE=0.25 /
  ITEM_DROP_CHANCE=0.20 (down from 0.70/0.40). On a hit, eligible content is
  filtered to CardDefinition.min_character_level / ItemDefinition.min_level
  <= killer's level, then a rarity tier is chosen by weight (common 60%,
  uncommon 25%, rare 12%, epic 3%, legendary 0% — legendaries never drop
  from trash mobs, reserved for bosses/dungeons) before sampling within
  tier. Empty tier -> falls back to the full eligible pool; empty pool ->
  no drop (never errors). Duplicate drops are intentional (merge fuel +
  spirit-sacrifice fodder), not a bug — see BALANCE.md.
end note

note bottom of Enemy
  **Tick logic (enemyTick, rules/, runs every 500ms):**
  IDLE -> CHASING if a player is within 300px (AGGRO_RANGE).
  CHASING -> move toward target at 110px/s (always slower than
    player's 180px/s, so a chase is always escapable);
    -> CASTING once within 180px (ATTACK_RANGE);
    -> RESETTING if target dies or leaves 500px (DEAGGRO_RANGE).
  CASTING -> telegraphed client-side; damage fires to every
    character still in attack_range_px once cast_duration_seconds
    elapses, then -> COOLDOWN.
  COOLDOWN -> recast (-> CASTING) after attack_cooldown_seconds
    if target still in range; re-chases if target moved out;
    resets if target died/left.
  RESETTING -> walk back to spawn_x/y at 80px/s, healing 10HP/tick;
    re-aggros if a player wanders in range; -> IDLE at spawn, full HP.
  Client interpolates pos_x/pos_y between server ticks.
end note

note as N_Derived
  **Computed in rules/, not stored:**
  effective_stats = race base + equipped gear, IMPLEMENTED in
  rules/stats.ts (computeRaceBase + computeEffectiveStats) and wired
  into resolveHit via index.ts#buildEffectiveStats. race base is
  currently a single hard-coded stub (computeRaceBase ignores its
  raceId arg) — the Race table/class above is still aspirational,
  no race_id column exists on Character yet. Still deferred: SET
  BONUSES (count equipped items sharing set_id vs pieces_required)
  and ward-passive card stats. Sets re-form each life (gear lost on
  death), so they must be repeatably attainable. CHAIN/EVOLUTION are
  content graphs over CardDefinition, giving skill-tree depth without
  point-buy.
end note

@enduml
